==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*6 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*8 [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Holy Valkyrie Cat (Enemy)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*4 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[General GreGory]] spawns after 130 seconds<sup>3,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Note that even though the requirement to access this stage is to complete [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 1, the [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] here are balanced around having all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from both Chapters 1 and 2 of Cats of the Cosmos. Even then, this stage should not be that difficult.

The UltraBaaBaas present here demand [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breakers]]... and that's the most difficult part of the stage. The Mistress Celeboodles serve to give you money, General Gregory is the main threat of the stage and has the capability to support Valkyrie incredibly well, but do remember, there's only 5 of them, and they are at 400% with all Crystal Treasures maxed. Once the fifth goes down (as long as you brought anything to stall Valkyrie) the stage is basically over. As mentioned before, the Starred Aliens meant to be fought after maxing CotC2 Crystal [[Treasure]]s so players should ideally have them at ≥900-1000% to stand a chance, and they become complete pushovers post-CotC3 since they'll barely even push. Sunfish Jones is there to prevent you from pushing too far. That leaves us with Holy Valkyrie Cat herself.

Holy Valkyrie Cat has a range of 350, meaning most [[:Category:Midranger-class Cats|midranger]]-[[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|backliner]] units can outrange her. Unlike her [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|allied counterpart]], she has a 75% chance to freeze units rather than 35%, so expect any cat with lower range than her to be constantly frozen. Note her high attack power, which doubles at 50% health, however she only attacks once every 4 seconds. Her high knockback count is both an advantage and a detriment to the player, as her high knockback count means she won't be able to hold the line if she does push, but its also high enough for you to easily push into Jones' range, which can be quite the nuisance.

Keeping all of this in mind, this stage is still relatively easy. As stated prior, any unit with a range above 350 will shine here, so [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]] variants can work. A viable strategy is to use [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] to stall her out and weaken her while your backliners chip her down. [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can work here, especially with its Extra Money [[Talents|Talent]] to snipe the peons before they become an issue. [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]], who has undoubtedly been useful throughout Cats of the Cosmos, proves to be useful here once again as a counter to UltraBaaBaa's [[Barrier]]. Other close range attackers like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] can be very helpful in chipping down the General GreGorys and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] are always a safe choice and any anti-Alien Ubers that can quickly dispose of the Gorys trivialise the stage.

Good Luck and may the freeze gods be with you.

